    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="69">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 69</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>CXIII. Sceap<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.27"/> sceal gongan mid his fliese<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.28"/> oð midne sumor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.29"/>; oððe gilde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.30"/> þæt flies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.31"/> mid twam pæningum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.32"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>S....al gongan...; oþþe... þæt flys ...</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="118" ed="#liebermann"/>CXIII. Sceap sceal gongan mid his flyse oð midne sumor; oððe gilde ðæt flys mid II penegum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Be sceapes gange. Sceap sceal gongan mid his flyse oð midne sumor; oððe gylde þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> fleos mid twa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> penegu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Ouis debet ire cum uellere suo usque ad mediam estatem; aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.17"/> persoluatur ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_69.lnote.oe.18"/> uellus II denariis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="58" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be sceapes gange.] Sceap sceal gongan mid his fliese oð midne sumor; oððe gilde þæt flies mid twam pæningum<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_69.attnote.fn.9"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="70" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="428" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CXIII} Sceap sceal gongan mid his fliese oð midne sumor; oððe gilde þæt flies mid twam pæningum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="119" ed="#liebermann"/>Ein Schaf soll mit seinem Vliess bis Mittsommer gehen; oder [wer es geschoren veräussert] ersetze das Vliess mit 2 Pfennigen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">A sheep is to go with its fleece until midsummer; or [whoever sells it shorn] let him make good the fleece with 2 pence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="59" ed="#attenborough"/>A sheep shall retain its fleece until midsummer. [If it is sheared before then], 2 pence shall be paid for the fleece<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_69.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="407" ed="#whitelock"/>A sheep must go with its fleece until midsummer, or else the fleece is to be paid for at twopence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="429" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>A sheep must go with its fleece until mid-summer, or the fleece must be recompensed with two pennies.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">119</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-pe <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-pe So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fleose <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> flyse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fleose So; flyse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-mer <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> somor <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-mer So; somor Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylde <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> gyld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylde So; gyld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fleos <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> fleose <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fleos Ld; fleose So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">118</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pen. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pen. So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_69.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Schaf 4. Eine Art der Veräusserung kann Hingabe als Zins an Grundherrn, Staat oder Kirche sein; Leo <hi rend="italic">Rectitudines</hi> 210. 1 Pfund Wolle (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1) wertet also 1—²/₃ Pfennig, wenn man die Schur eines Schafes zu 2—3 Pfund annimmt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Schaf 4. One kind of alienation may be handing it over as rent to a landlord, the state or the church; Leo <hi rend="italic">Rectitudines</hi> 210. 1 pound of wool (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1) is therefore worth 1—²/₃ penny, if one takes the fleece of one sheep to be 2—3 pounds</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_69.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><label>pæningum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">penegum</hi>. B &amp; H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_69.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> by anyone who sells a sheep which has been shorn before that date. This would mean that two pence would be deducted from the price of the sheep.</seg></note>
      </div>
